# Certified-assets has NO default security headers, unlike the legacy asset canister's
# `security_policy: "standard"`. These reproduce that policy's seven headers verbatim,
# with three deliberate tightenings — this page takes card details, so the baseline is
# not negotiable and a copy-paste CSP that breaks the app is worse than none.
#
# ⚠️ **This CARRIES the headers over; it does not introduce them.** Measured by
# redeploying the legacy recipe and curling: it served all seven. `scripts/e2e-local.sh`
# asserts each one, because nothing else can — the browser suite serves `dist` from a
# static server, where `_headers` never applies.
# ⚠️ **The `icp0.io` entries in `connect-src` are NOT the derivation origin** (that is
# `src/frontend/src/config.ts`, and II fetches it rather than this page). They predate
# `agentOptions` omitting `host` on mainnet: calls now go to `https://icp-api.io`, which is
# listed, and a page served from a canister URL or a custom domain is covered by `'self'`.
# So they look dead. Left in place rather than removed on that reasoning alone, because
# narrowing a CSP is only safe once a mainnet deployment has exercised every call path.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self';script-src 'self';connect-src 'self' http://localhost:* https://icp0.io https://*.icp0.io https://icp-api.io;img-src 'self' data:;style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';style-src-elem 'self' 'unsafe-inline';font-src 'self';object-src 'none';base-uri 'self';frame-ancestors 'none';form-action 'self';upgrade-insecure-requests;
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), autoplay=(), battery=(), camera=(), cross-origin-isolated=(), display-capture=(), document-domain=(), encrypted-media=(), execution-while-not-rendered=(), execution-while-out-of-viewport=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), keyboard-map=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), navigation-override=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), sync-xhr=(), usb=(), web-share=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), clipboard-read=(), clipboard-write=(), gamepad=(), speaker-selection=(), conversion-measurement=(), focus-without-user-activation=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), interest-cohort=(), serial=(), sync-script=(), trust-token-redemption=(), window-placement=(), vertical-scroll=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block

# Vite content-hashes everything here, so it can never go stale.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML revalidates so a deploy is picked up. Patterns match the ASSET KEY, not the
# visitor URL — `/` is served from `/index.html`, so this is the block that governs it.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Not content-hashed, so it needs a rule of its own: long enough to stop a refetch on
# every navigation, short enough that a brand change is not stuck in caches for a year.
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# ⚠️ Internet Identity fetches this and parses it as JSON, and the file has no extension,
# so nothing infers a type for it. The bare `Content-Type:` form sets the asset's stored
# media type rather than adding a response header.
#
# It is served from the DERIVATION origin (the canister URL, see src/frontend/src/config.ts)
# and lists every domain allowed to derive principals from it. A serving domain missing
# from this list has its sign-in refused by II, not silently given a different principal.
/.well-known/ii-alternative-origins
  Content-Type: application/json

# The custom-domain claim the boundary nodes read. `.well-known/` is uploaded by the
# static-site plugin automatically; every other dot-path is skipped.
/.well-known/ic-domains
  Content-Type: text/plain
